The v0.15.1 probe that wrote ../v0151-generated.json and ../v0151-realistic.json.

It is not built with this tree (testdata/ is outside every package). It runs inside a v0.15.1
checkout, against v0.15.1's own config load, validation and loophole resolution:

    git archive -o v0151.tar v0.15.1      # then untar it into a scratch directory, v0151/
    mkdir v0151/cmd/lcaccept && cp main.go v0151/cmd/lcaccept/
    cd v0151
    go run -mod=vendor ./cmd/lcaccept <this dir>/candidates.json > v0151-generated.json
    go run -mod=vendor ./cmd/lcaccept <this dir>/candidates.json <this dir>/../realistic > v0151-realistic.json

The first form generates the per-key cases (every top-level key in candidates.json at user and
workspace scope; every loophole switch at user scope, workspace scope and in the per-workspace
file; every declared loophole setting at its declared scope), keeps those v0.15.1 accepted and
records what v0.15.1 made of each. Refused cases go to stderr. The second judges the realistic
case trees the same way, skipping those marked current_only.

The probe runs v0.15.1's ValidateConfig, not its launch's capability gate, so it reports the
toplevel/required_capabilities cases as accepted; v0.15.1's launch refused them (nothing satisfies
the sample capability), and they were removed from v0151-generated.json by hand.

Run it with YOLO_VERSION unset and TMPDIR on a disk that survives the run; it leaves its temporary
homes behind, because v0.15.1 leases its embedded pack tree under the first HOME it sees.
